# A09 construction history (before preregistration; formal candidate/auditor/retry=0/0/0)

Builder attempt 1 exposed a construction gate defect: all 24 approach cases accidentally retained one fixed cadence (intervals 350/450/475/325 ms), despite the intended irregular-per-case design. It was caught by an explicit cadence-diversity check before any preregistration or formal role invocation. Observed output digests: manifest `8d266d65abc7e88e1e7aacf17bcdbd10e3b8d4fbcea5f9e10a725e052a233773`, truth `2fcf03dc4e7540310366dc4e8c1974ff35e41e8ba1f1681db854ef1d4f1dba14`; the initial shell reported generator SHA `ac00e7289da60f337a10294c73464b7e1aa7179c5445c725dd24de94eade947b`. The initial source bytes were not captured at that moment. A reconstructed builder at SHA `5e94b2f73857d51d0b5e6252523114e77684dead2503e99444391fc712dbbf5c` reproduced both output digests and the same one-cadence finding. This records the construction custody limitation; neither source nor output was exposed to a candidate.

Correction before preregistration: add per-approach seeded interval jitter to a fresh corrected generator (SHA recorded in FREEZE.json), and use fresh seed 20261007. Corrected builder produced 30 sequences/150 frames, 24 distinct approach cadence tuples, 30 opaque IDs, and no class/contact field in candidate-visible manifest. Corrected manifest SHA `27a1cca57c00dfbc0a1ee41d14abcfe29175ff39449d2704ff8c7f4e73e78b43`; sealed truth SHA `c8f9ed461b9388455cc3be42496f14c152afc1b982b1bba890c8c58ca446b5b0`.

A separate network-disabled pinned-image mount preflight mounted only observations read-only at `/input`, read `/input/manifest.json` and all 30 opaque cases, and reported `cpu.max=100000 100000`, `memory.max=max`, `memory.swap.max=max`. This is construction only. No candidate, auditor, model, game, GPU or input authority was used. `--cpus 1` is enforced as one CPU here; memory/swap remain unlimited.

